{#
  snowflake-jdbc bundles Apache Arrow, which reflectively accesses
  java.nio.Buffer's internal address field for off-heap memory access. The
  JDK 9+ module system blocks that by default, so without this flag the
  driver fails with InaccessibleObjectException as soon as it tries to
  decode an Arrow result. Maven reads .mvn/jvm.config automatically on
  startup (see https://maven.apache.org/configure.html#mvn-jvm-config-file),
  so this applies to `mvn compile exec:java` without changing the
  invocation. The file is passed verbatim as JVM arguments -- it does not
  support comments, so this note lives in the Jinja template instead.
-#}
{%- if engine == "snowflake" -%}
--add-opens=java.base/java.nio=ALL-UNNAMED
{%- endif -%}
